    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0743" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8830 Brazil/241: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-14T15:00:00-03:00">June 14, 1943—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2874. For Rockefeller,<anchor n="57" xml:id="d689-f1"/> McClintock and
                        Rovensky<anchor n="58" xml:id="d689-f2"/> from Friele.<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d689-f3"/> Foodstuffs shortage Bahia and other northeastern ports
                    creating critical situation for whole propaganda position, since blame being
                    placed Americans. Food Production Division contributing splendidly but time
                    factor makes shipping problem extremely important for immediate future. Embassy
                    detailed situation in telegram 2769 of June 7, 7 p.m. We strongly urge you lend
                    every possible immediate support those recommendations. [Friele.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d689-f1" n="57" xml:id="d689-f1-content">
                <p>Nelson A. Rockefeller, Coordinator of Inter-American Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d689-f2" n="58" xml:id="d689-f2-content">
                <p>John C. McClintock and Joseph C. Rovensky, Assistant Coordinators of
                    Inter-American Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d689-f3" n="59" xml:id="d689-f3-content">
                <p>Berent Friele, Representative of the Coordinator of Inter-American Affairs in
                    Brazil.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
